  "body": "The following yields three results in three browsers:\r\n```html\r\n<!doctype html>\r\n<p id=log></p>\r\n<script>\r\nvar log = s => document.getElementById(\"log\").textContent += s;\r\nvar source = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\r\ncreateImageBitmap(source, 0, 0, 100000000, 100000000)\r\n  .then(x => log(`resolved with ${x} (w=${x.width}, h=${x.height})`),\r\n        e => log(`rejected with ${e}`))\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\nBrowser   | Output\r\n----------|------------\r\nChrome    | [rejected with InvalidStateError: The ImageBitmap could not be allocated.](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=799025)\r\nFirefox   | resolved with [object ImageBitmap] (w=100000000, h=100000000)\r\nWebKitGTK | resolved with [object ImageBitmap] (w=300, h=150)\r\n",
